# A1: the AUDITED eight-seat 262k attach of the whole wave-2 stack on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2-audit: the W1 audited profile (every audit of wave 1: the drafter conv and heads, the unit-major reduce-scatter, the host-gap full read-back with its 1c shadow, the fused commit, the verify glue, the draft singles)
# plus the two wave-2 audits: QWEN_FAST_TP4_SDPA_AUDIT=1 (the per-user SDPA launches run beside the multi launch in every attention layer and a device kernel compares the two block outputs word for word) and QWEN_FAST_TP4_CONV_GATES_SPREAD_AUDIT=1 (the served conv-gates op runs on
# cloned windows beside the F1 launch and conv, beta, g and the four advanced windows are compared with the launch's on EVERY chip as int16 bit patterns, riding the verify-glue audit). THE FIRST ATTACH OF SDPA multi WITH WAVE 1 (they were never run together). The verify T1/T2 audits stay OFF as in the W1 audited arm.
# The smoke runs concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix) and concurrent8_code_32k. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) the attach: every W1 lever engaged (prestage mode=blocks on both blocks, block epochs, tp4 u1 unit_major above 0, draft conv, draft heads), NO "[PINDIAG] packed sampler arm" line (nosamp took effect),
# '[PINDIAG] tp4 sdpa engaged' with config=multi flags=0x21 AND the '[PINDIAG] tp4 sdpa multi call' line (built is not executed), '[PINDIAG] tp4 conv gates spread engaged' with gate_cores=2 and per_core equal to served_per_core, and NO refused or fell-back line of any lever
# ('[PINDIAG] tp4 conv gates spread fell back' names the reason: a source that is not the pinned one, an operand layout, a grid without room: each is a finding); (2) ZERO audit mismatches of every kind: the W1 audit lines of tp4-w1-jobs A1, '[PINDIAG] tp4 sdpa audit' lines with exact=True and none MISMATCH, '[PINDIAG] tp4 conv gates spread audit <n> exact=True layers=... entries=...'
# with a multiple of 7 entries per audited layer and no 'audit mismatch' line; (3) c2_smoke_check clean; (4) every answer's content hash equal to S0c's on concurrent8_code_32k and concurrent8_code_equal.
# INTERACTION READ: the SDPA audit's per-user launches and the F1 audit's served call add launches of their own to the trace; a capture-order or L1 finding that shows only here is read against the wave-1 audited arm first (tp4-w1-jobs A1), then the levers one at a time. Duration (estimate): 180 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 eight-seat 262k wave-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w2 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
